# ============================================================================
# kd-server — AI test file (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client)
# ============================================================================
#
# SETUP
#   1. In .env set your key (this alone enables AI — no encryption key needed):
#        ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#        # AI_DEFAULT_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8   # optional, if your key can't reach sonnet-5
#   2. Start the server:  go run ./cmd/api
#      The startup banner must show:  AI: enabled (anthropic) — server default key set
#      If it says "not configured", ANTHROPIC_API_KEY isn't set / not loaded.
#   3. Copy this file to ai.rest (gitignored) and set the admin values below.
#   4. Run the requests in Section 1 top-to-bottom (the login cookie is reused).
# ============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:18080

# Admin credentials — must match KD_ADMIN_USERNAME / KD_ADMIN_PASSWORD in .env
@adminUser = admin
@adminPass = generate-a-strong-random-password


# ============================================================================
# SECTION 1 — Test the env key (no encryption key needed). RUN IN ORDER.
# ============================================================================

### 1a. Admin login — stores the session cookie for the requests below.
# Expect: 200 {"status":"authenticated"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{adminUser}}", "password": "{{adminPass}}" }

### 1b. Is AI active, and where does the key come from?
# Expect: 200 {"configured":true,"paired":true,"source":"env","key_hint":"...XXXX",...}
#   "source":"env" = using your ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
#   404 = AI not active (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY not set / wrong branch).
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/api/ai-status

### 1c. Live check — actually calls Anthropic with the current key.
# Expect: 200 {"ok":true,"provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-sonnet-5"}
#   400 "api key rejected by provider" = bad key, or the model isn't on your plan
#        (set AI_DEFAULT_MODEL to one you have, e.g. claude-haiku-4-5, and restart).
#   400 "no default key configured" = ANTHROPIC_API_KEY not set.
#   502 = couldn't reach Anthropic (network).
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/api/ai-validate

# If 1c is 200, AI is working — upload an ID card in the /admin extract box and
# the response "engine" will be "anthropic:<model>" instead of "tesseract-5".


# ============================================================================
# SECTION 2 — Store keys in the DB (only if AI_ENCRYPTION_KEY is set)
# ============================================================================
# These persist an encrypted key. They require AI_ENCRYPTION_KEY in .env; without
# it they return 400 "set AI_ENCRYPTION_KEY". Not needed for the env-key flow above.

# Fill these for the tenant flow:
@tenant = pem
@tenantKey = key_yourKeyId.yourSecret
@anthropicKey = sk-ant-REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_KEY

### 2a. Admin: pair a server-default key (encrypted). Powers extraction like the env key.
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/api/ai-credentials
Content-Type: application/json

{ "api_key": "{{anthropicKey}}", "model": "claude-sonnet-5" }

### 2b. Admin: unpair the stored default key.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/api/ai-credentials

### 2c. Tenant: store a per-tenant key (Bearer auth).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/ai/credentials
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantKey}}
X-KD-Tenant: {{tenant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "api_key": "{{anthropicKey}}", "model": "claude-sonnet-5" }

### 2d. Tenant: list stored keys (masked).
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/ai/credentials
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantKey}}
X-KD-Tenant: {{tenant}}

### 2e. Tenant: delete the stored key.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/ai/credentials/anthropic
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantKey}}
X-KD-Tenant: {{tenant}}


# ============================================================================
# SECTION 3 — Sanity
# ============================================================================

### Public health check — no auth. Expect: 200 {"ok":true}
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/healthz
